2026-07-09 22:22:23,946 DEBUG text: This is the disaster analysis report for Ballari, Karnataka, India, generated on 09 July 2026 at 10:22 PM. The location lies in the Equatorial Region, an area typically prone to Heavy Rainfall, Floods, Landslides. Current weather conditions show a temperature of 26.6 degrees Celsius, wind speeds of 16.8 kilometers per hour, and rainfall of 0.0 millimeters over the past six hours. The flood risk for this location is assessed as no flood risk, with a flood prediction of no risk. The nearest recorded earthquake occurred near 7 km SE of Parbhani, India with a magnitude of 4.2, placing the earthquake risk at medium. No volcanic activity was detected in the surrounding region. Combining these factors, the overall disaster risk for this location is classified as medium. The emergency response system has been activated. 6 hospitals and medical facilities, 6 shelters, and 4 food and relief resources were identified within the response radius. The nearest hospital is St. Mary's Medical Center (6), approximately 7.4 kilometers away. Ambulance stations, police, fire services, blood banks, and coordination with local non-governmental organizations and rescue teams have also been factored into the response plan. Moderate earthquake activity detected: stay alert for aftershocks and avoid unsafe or older structures. Nearest hospital identified: St. Mary's Medical Center (6) (7.4 km away) — keep this location on hand. Follow the recommended safe evacuation route, proceeding via: Start, then SafeZone1, then SafeZone2. Stay tuned to official government and disaster management channels for updates. Keep an emergency kit ready with essential supplies, water, and medication. Overall, Ballari is currently assessed at MEDIUM disaster risk, corresponding to a preparedness level of Level 2 - Elevated. Heightened readiness advised. Monitor conditions closely and prepare contingency plans. Emergency response resources have been identified and are detailed in this report. Continued monitoring is advised as conditions may change. Stay safe and prepared.
