2026-07-09 22:22:52,973 DEBUG text: This is the disaster analysis report for Dharwad, Karnataka, India, generated on 09 July 2026 at 10:22 PM. The location lies in the Equatorial Region, an area typically prone to Heavy Rainfall, Floods, Landslides. Current weather conditions show a temperature of 22.7 degrees Celsius, wind speeds of 16.0 kilometers per hour, and rainfall of 0.0 millimeters over the past six hours. The flood risk for this location is assessed as low, with a flood prediction of low. The nearest recorded earthquake occurred near 7 km SE of Parbhani, India with a magnitude of 4.2, placing the earthquake risk at medium. No volcanic activity was detected in the surrounding region. Combining these factors, the overall disaster risk for this location is classified as high. The emergency response system has been activated. 10 hospitals and medical facilities, 9 shelters, and 9 food and relief resources were identified within the response radius. The nearest hospital is Dharwad Community Health Center (7), approximately 2.5 kilometers away. Ambulance stations, police, fire services, blood banks, and coordination with local non-governmental organizations and rescue teams have also been factored into the response plan. Moderate earthquake activity detected: stay alert for aftershocks and avoid unsafe or older structures. Low flood risk detected: remain cautious of localized flooding, especially in low-lying zones. Nearest hospital identified: Dharwad Community Health Center (7) (2.5 km away) — keep this location on hand. Follow the recommended safe evacuation route, proceeding via: Start, then SafeZone1, then SafeZone2. Stay tuned to official government and disaster management channels for updates. Keep an emergency kit ready with essential supplies, water, and medication. Overall, Dharwad is currently assessed at HIGH disaster risk, corresponding to a preparedness level of Level 3 - Critical. Immediate action required. Activate full emergency response protocols and follow evacuation guidance without delay. Emergency response resources have been identified and are detailed in this report. Continued monitoring is advised as conditions may change. Stay safe and prepared.
