2026-07-10 22:38:07,424 DEBUG text: This is the disaster analysis report for Udupi, Karnataka, India, generated on 10 July 2026 at 10:38 PM. The location lies in the Equatorial Region, an area typically prone to Heavy Rainfall, Floods, Landslides. Current weather conditions show a temperature of 25.6 degrees Celsius, wind speeds of 2.8 kilometers per hour, and rainfall of 1.6 millimeters over the past six hours. The flood risk for this location is assessed as medium, with a flood prediction of medium. No significant recent earthquake activity was detected nearby. No volcanic activity was detected in the surrounding region. Combining these factors, the overall disaster risk for this location is classified as medium. The emergency response system has been activated. 4 hospitals and medical facilities, 5 shelters, and 7 food and relief resources were identified within the response radius. The nearest hospital is Udupi Community Health Center, approximately 8.7 kilometers away. Ambulance stations, police, fire services, blood banks, and coordination with local non-governmental organizations and rescue teams have also been factored into the response plan. Moderate flood risk detected: monitor rising water levels closely and prepare an evacuation plan. Nearest hospital identified: Udupi Community Health Center (8.7 km away) — keep this location on hand. Follow the recommended safe evacuation route, proceeding via: Start, then SafeZone1, then SafeZone2. Stay tuned to official government and disaster management channels for updates. Keep an emergency kit ready with essential supplies, water, and medication. Overall, Udupi is currently assessed at MEDIUM disaster risk, corresponding to a preparedness level of Level 2 - Elevated. Heightened readiness advised. Monitor conditions closely and prepare contingency plans. Emergency response resources have been identified and are detailed in this report. Continued monitoring is advised as conditions may change. Stay safe and prepared.
